Z||000003||theogre||04-19-2000||08:42 PM||||Is it just local to me or do the passenger side ones always look way worse than the drivers?<P>I'm in the middle of preping one for a repaint. It's sooooo pitted. I'm overlaying epoxy onto it. That should make it next to indestructabele as far as finish. I'll make the last coats a black epoxy then prime and paint it. Even if all the paint comes off the epoxy never will. Too bad you can't get a satin finish epoxy paint. ||||reg||1
Z||000004||CUTTER||04-20-2000||04:11 AM||||haha, I dont have to worry about a passenger side mirror because I dont have one from a recent side swipe from a fence over the winter...should of never drove it on a cold icy night!!!!<BR>  Shane, blue 87GT  "Watch out for them fences"||||reg||1
Z||000005||phillip||04-20-2000||09:41 AM||||could you explain that epoxy stuff. what is it and how do you you work with it. i put a pair or motorcycle mirrors on mine off a ninja (i think) and one looks a little rough.||||reg||1
Z||000006||theogre||04-20-2000||12:05 PM||||Epoxy is allot tougher than body fillers in this application. It is also structural so if any pits are pin holed the Epxoy will provide a stable paint base that's unlikely to crack out.<P>epoxy is a 2 part adhesive. Most come are 1:1 mix. add equall amounts of each tube and stir. (Epoxy Paint on the other hand is not usually a 1:1 mix. Mix it as directed.)<P>In this case I'm using a standard clear resin to fill the pits. It's just a standard adhesive that comes in a binarry plunger tube. Set time is around 10 minutes. (Use something with slower setup time if you aren't used to working with Epoxy. Working time is about 1/3-1/2 setting time depending on temperature.) I just mix the epoxy and use something stiff to spread it really thin over the mirror shell. Spread it as thin as posible. (Most of it has been sanded off. It's there to fill the pits.)<P>I'd like to find a black resin and use that as a base layer for the paint. Might use a black marine epoxy paint. I might even be able to get that in a sattin finish in which case I don't need to use automotive paint.||||reg||1
Z||000007||lowCG||04-20-2000||06:10 PM||||Krylon(Sherwin Williams product)has been the best I've found.Had the surface wiped with alcohol,warmed up with a hair dryer,and heated the paint in warm water before spraying,and shook it up alot too.Three good coats,waiting a day in between coats,and wet sanding lightly before spraying all helped to create the bond.<BR>||||reg||3
Z||000008||1FieroGTRacingInc||04-22-2000||07:16 AM||||OK Guy's... the Question was .. Do they make Bra's for the mirror's??  DO THEY??<BR>                   1FieroGTRacingInc.||||reg||1
